{"agent":"lane-su","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_by_name` treats any non-list as an empty inventory, so a missing digest is reported as a hard upgrade. Given `served=None` (no `tools/list` yet) and `live=[{\"name\": \"doctor\", \"description\": \"x\"}]`, `delta` returns one added tool and `RestartNotice.footer(\"unknown\", None, live)` returns `ddflow was upgraded (1 tool added): restart your agent to see it`. Given `served=[{\"name\": \"doctor\"}]` and `live=None`, `removed_tool(\"doctor\", served, None, name_chars=64)` returns the upgrade-removed string even though the worker list was never loaded.","digest":"453cbed44838a05f","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/mcpshim/notice.py:39","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/mcpshim/notice.py:39"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"A call to a removed tool does not return the shared upgrade `message`. For served `[{\"name\": \"old_tool\", \"inputSchema\": {}}]` and live `[]`, `message(delta(...))` is `ddflow was upgraded (1 removed): restart your agent to see it`, but `removed_tool(\"old_tool\", ...)` returns `tool 'old_tool' was removed by a ddflow upgrade: restart your agent to see the current tools`. That is not the doctor/SessionStart line the notice is specified to reuse.","digest":"583f57ddd55d3c51","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/mcpshim/notice.py:91","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/mcpshim/notice.py:91"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12827,"diff_sha":"078b9bdc2cf18b7962c3b3068b79604e8663b1cd330e00a713911154ca37f17f","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/SU-restart-notice","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":128.3,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"5e59ee4eb17a06f5","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/